+# bookmarks 1.0.0
+
+Manage bookmarks
+
+Implementations print each help text below exactly, to stdout, and exit with 0 (`-h` and `--help`). See `docs/design/rules.md` OPS-05.
+
+## Usage
+
+```text
+Usage: bookmarks <noun> <verb> [options]
+
+Manage bookmarks
+
+Commands:
+  bookmark create  Create a bookmark
+  bookmark delete  Delete a bookmark
+  bookmark edit    Edit a bookmark
+  bookmark list    List bookmarks
+  bookmark view    View a bookmark
+
+Options:
+  -h, --help     Show help
+      --version  Show the version
+```
+
+## Commands
+
+### bookmarks bookmark create
+
+```text
+Usage: bookmarks bookmark create [options]
+
+Create a bookmark
+
+Options:
+  -h, --help         Show help
+      --json         Write the output as JSON
+      --tag TAG      Tag of the bookmark (repeatable)
+      --title TITLE  Title of the bookmark (required)
+      --url URL      Url of the bookmark (required)
+```
+
+- Output: one `bookmark`
+- Exit codes: 0, 1, 2
+
+### bookmarks bookmark delete
+
+```text
+Usage: bookmarks bookmark delete [options] <id>
+
+Delete a bookmark
+
+Arguments:
+  <id>  ID of the bookmark
+
+Options:
+  -h, --help  Show help
+      --json  Write the output as JSON
+```
+
+- Output: one `bookmark`
+- Exit codes: 0, 1, 2, 3
+
+### bookmarks bookmark edit
+
+```text
+Usage: bookmarks bookmark edit [options] <id>
+
+Edit a bookmark
+
+Arguments:
+  <id>  ID of the bookmark
+
+Options:
+  -h, --help         Show help
+      --json         Write the output as JSON
+      --tag TAG      New tag of the bookmark (repeatable)
+      --title TITLE  New title of the bookmark
+      --url URL      New url of the bookmark
+```
+
+- Output: one `bookmark`
+- Exit codes: 0, 1, 2, 3
+
+### bookmarks bookmark list
+
+```text
+Usage: bookmarks bookmark list [options]
+
+List bookmarks
+
+Options:
+  -h, --help         Show help
+      --json         Write the output as JSON
+      --limit LIMIT  Maximum number of bookmarks to show (default: 20)
+      --sort SORT    Field to sort the bookmarks by (one of: created_at, id, title, updated_at, url; default: id)
+      --tag TAG      Show only bookmarks with this tag (repeatable)
+```
+
+- Output: a list of `bookmark`
+- Exit codes: 0, 1, 2
+
+### bookmarks bookmark view
+
+```text
+Usage: bookmarks bookmark view [options] <id>
+
+View a bookmark
+
+Arguments:
+  <id>  ID of the bookmark
+
+Options:
+  -h, --help  Show help
+      --json  Write the output as JSON
+```
+
+- Output: one `bookmark`
+- Exit codes: 0, 1, 2, 3
+
+## Output types
+
+`--json` writes an object with every field in this order, or an array of such objects. Text output is a table whose header is the field names in upper case.
+
+### bookmark
+
+| Field | Type | Nullable |
+|---|---|---|
+| `id` | integer | no |
+| `created_at` | timestamp | no |
+| `tags` | list of string | no |
+| `title` | string | no |
+| `updated_at` | timestamp | no |
+| `url` | string | no |
+
+## Exit codes
+
+| Code | Meaning |
+|---|---|
+| 0 | Success |
+| 1 | Unexpected failure, such as a file that cannot be read or written |
+| 2 | Invalid usage, such as an unknown option or a value of the wrong type |
+| 3 | The specified item, file, or directory does not exist |
+
+## Environment variables
+
+| Name | Type | Default | Description |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `BOOKMARKS_DATA_DIR` | directory | `$XDG_DATA_HOME/bookmarks` | Directory for data files |
+
+A value given by an option takes precedence over the environment variable, which takes precedence over the default.
+
+## Data directory
+
+The first of these that applies is used. It is created with permission 0700 if it does not exist.
+
+1. `BOOKMARKS_DATA_DIR`, if it is a non-empty absolute path
+2. Linux and macOS: `$XDG_DATA_HOME/bookmarks`, if `XDG_DATA_HOME` is a non-empty absolute path. Windows: `%LOCALAPPDATA%\bookmarks`
+3. Linux and macOS: `$HOME/.local/share/bookmarks`
+
+## Version
+
+`bookmarks --version` prints `bookmarks 1.0.0` and exits with 0.
